# tc conventions (Cursor rule)

Canonical, always-authoritative sources — read them before writing code:
- `@AGENTS.md`
- `@docs/agents/STYLE.md` (the prescriptive style guide — most important)
- `@docs/agents/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `@docs/agents/DSL.md`
- `@docs/agents/CALIBRATION.md`

Conformance to the existing style is the acceptance criterion — matching the
author's conventions matters as much as correctness.

## Always
- Small, terse **free functions** over methods/`impl`. Take `&Topology`/`&Auth`/
  `&str`, return owned `String`/`Vec`/`HashMap`.
- Use the **`kit`** crate: `use kit as u;` + `use kit::*;`. Prefer `s()`, `empty()`,
  `s!`, `v!`, `maybe_*`, `nth`, `split*` over inline logic.
- Fail-fast error handling: `.unwrap()`, `.expect("fail")`, `panic!`. Graceful
  degradation **only** in the caching/concurrency layer (`kit::memo`, resolver
  concurrency, `differ`).
- Data structs: `#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Clone, Debug)]`, all fields `pub`,
  `HashMap<String, _>`-of-everything, `Option<T>` + `#[serde(default)]`.
- Bounded concurrency (`buffer_unordered(n)`, env-configurable cap clamped to a
  `const` ceiling). Config via `TC_*` env vars.
- Imports crate-granular + vertical (nightly `rustfmt`). Add a `#[cfg(test)]` twin
  for any new leaf IO fn.
- Respect `TopologySpec` (unresolved, `Option`) vs `Topology` (resolved, `HashMap`).

## Never
- Add `anyhow`, `thiserror`, or a custom error enum.
- Introduce a provider trait/abstraction (AWS is hard-coded by design).
- "Modernize" intentional idioms: keep `.clone()`s, `x.len() > 0`, `match opt {..}`;
  do not convert free functions to methods; do not reformat unrelated files.
- Add dependencies or move responsibilities between crates without discussing it.

## Before finishing
Run `./scripts/agent-check.sh` (nightly fmt on changed files, line-scoped clippy,
`cargo build`, `cargo test -p composer`, convention greps). The full `cargo test
--workspace` suite is green as of Phase 2 (CI runs it) — see CALIBRATION.md.
